Long ago, when the world was young, the night sky was completely dark. The Moon ruled alone, proud and luminous, casting silver light upon the sleeping earth.

One day, the Sun challenged the Moon's importance. "I bring warmth and life," he boasted. "What do you offer but cold reflection?"

