Wounded, the Moon wept. Her tears fell through darkness and froze into crystalline points of light—the first stars. When the Sun saw what his pride had wrought, shame filled his heart.

"Forgive me," he whispered. "Your tears have created something beautiful."

The Moon smiled through her sorrow. "Let them remain as stars, reminding all that beauty can emerge from pain."

But the youngest stars were curious. "Why do we exist?" they asked the Moon.

"You are here to witness," she replied. "Watch over those below, guide the lost, and remind the lonely they are never truly alone in darkness."

The smallest star worried. "What if my light is too dim to matter?"

The Moon touched her gently. "Every light matters. Together, you transform the night from emptiness into wonder. One star may seem small, but thousands together create hope."

Since then, stars have filled the darkness, each one a reminder that every small light contributes to something magnificent.

